# GitHub highlights with the grammars Linguist carries, and Alloy is not
# one of them yet. Luau is, and the two share their shape, so a file
# reads well there: the words Alloy adds stay plain. The editor uses the
# real grammar, in alloy-luau/extensions.
*.aly linguist-language=Luau
*.alx linguist-language=Luau

# The golden cases are fixtures of the compiler's own tests. They read
# as code, and they say nothing about what this crate is written in.
alloy/tests/cases/** linguist-detectable=false
